@startuml 10-lost-pet-amap-and-claim-handover-sequence
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFDF9
skinparam defaultFontName "PingFang SC, Inter, sans-serif"
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam SequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ArrowColor #5C534E

title F09 Lost Pet Coarse Coordinate Privacy (GCJ-02/WGS-84), Amap Proxy, Nearby Matching & Bilateral Claim Handover

actor "Pet Owner" as Owner
actor "Community Finder" as Finder
participant "Client UI & LostMap\n(Android MapView / iOS MAMapView /\nWeb AmapView / Desktop Browser Handoff)" as Client
participant "Amap Reverse Proxy\n(mobileapi.ServeAmapProxy\n/maps/amap/_AMapService/)" as AmapProxy
participant "AutoNavi AMap Cloud" as ExtAmap
participant "Go API\n(mobile.Service)" as Api
database "PostgreSQL\n(mobile_lost_reports /\nmobile_sighting_clues /\nmobile_lost_claims)" as Db

== 1. Amap Privacy Compliance & 2-Decimal Coarse Coordinate Quantization ==
Owner -> Client : Open LostMap Page -> Accept Amap Privacy Notice
Client -> Client : Native: MapsInitializer.updatePrivacyShow/Agree (Android) /\nMAMapView.updatePrivacyShow/Agree (iOS)\nQuantize selected coordinate to 2 decimal places (~1.1 km grid):\ncoarseLat = round(lat, 2), coarseLng = round(lng, 2), datum = "GCJ-02" | "WGS-84"

opt Web Map Tile / Reverse Geocode Request
  Client -> AmapProxy : GET /maps/amap/_AMapService/v3/geocode/regeo?location=116.40,39.91
  AmapProxy -> ExtAmap : Forward request with server-injected `jscode` (securityJsCode never exposed to browser)
  ExtAmap --> AmapProxy : Geocode JSON
  AmapProxy --> Client : Sanitized Geocode JSON
end

== 2. Publish Lost Pet Report with Coarse Public Marker ==
Owner -> Client : Submit Lost Report (petId, coarseLat, coarseLng, datum="GCJ-02", lastSeenAreaText)
Client -> Api : POST /api/v2/lost-reports\n{petId, coarseLat: 31.23, coarseLng: 121.47, datum: "GCJ-02", areaLabel, rewardNote}
Api -> Api : Enforce 2-decimal truncation & reject high-precision raw GPS fields
Api -> Db : INSERT mobile_lost_reports (status='active', datum='GCJ-02', coarse_lat=31.23, coarse_lng=121.47)
Api --> Client : 201 LostReportView (Public marker visible on LostMap)

== 3. Same-Datum Nearby Query & Sighting Clue Submission ==
Finder -> Client : Browse LostMap in Shanghai (datum="GCJ-02", viewport center 31.23, 121.47)
Client -> Api : GET /api/v2/lost-reports/nearby?datum=GCJ-02&lat=31.23&lng=121.47&radiusKm=15
Api -> Db : Query active reports WHERE datum = 'GCJ-02' within bounding box\n(Never mixes GCJ-02 and WGS-84 without explicit datum filter)
Db --> Api : Matching coarse LostReport markers
Api --> Client : 200 LostReportListResponse

Finder -> Client : Submit Sighting Clue or Found Claim with photo evidence
Client -> Api : POST /api/v2/lost-reports/{reportId}/claims\n{evidenceMediaIds, finderNote, coarseLat, coarseLng, datum}
Api -> Db : INSERT mobile_lost_claims (status='pending_owner_review')\n(Exact contact/meetup details kept private until owner accepts claim)
Api --> Client : 201 LostClaimView

== 4. Private Claim Verification, Context-Bound Appointment & Bilateral Handover ==
Owner -> Client : Review Claim Evidence & Accept for Verification
Client -> Api : POST /api/v2/lost-reports/{reportId}/claims/{claimId}/accept-review
Api -> Db : UPDATE mobile_lost_claims SET status='in_handover'\nUnlock private conversation & context-bound appointment (context_type='lost_claim')
Api --> Client : 200 LostClaimView (status='in_handover')

Finder -> Api : POST /api/v2/lost-reports/{reportId}/claims/{claimId}/confirm-handover (Finder confirms)
Owner -> Api : POST /api/v2/lost-reports/{reportId}/claims/{claimId}/confirm-handover (Owner confirms with Reauth)
Api -> Db : BEGIN SERIALIZABLE\n1. Mark mobile_lost_claims status='completed_reunited'\n2. Mark mobile_lost_reports status='resolved_reunited' (removed from public active map)\n3. Archive other pending claims on same reportId\nCOMMIT
Api --> Owner : 200 LostReportView (status='resolved_reunited')

@enduml
